{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AI Assistant for Enterprise – Amazon Q Business Pricing – AWS","context":"### Subscription pricing\n\nWith Amazon Q Business, enterprise customers pay for user subscriptions and index capacity. Choose from two subscription models, Amazon Q Business Lite and Amazon Q Business Pro, to meet your needs.\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Amazon Q Business Lite**$3 per user/mo.The Amazon Q Business Lite subscription provides users access to basic functionality such as asking questions and receiving permission-aware responses. * Securely connect Amazon Q Business to your business knowledge and data * Receive permission-aware responses in a conversational interface (responses up to approximately one page) * Use secure and seamless sign-on with enterprise login * Gain fast insights on your uploaded files * Access Q Business through the web browser extension | **Amazon Q Business Pro**$20 per user/mo.The Amazon Q Business Pro subscription provides users access to the full suite of Amazon Q Business capabilities, including access to Amazon Q Apps, and Amazon Q in QuickSight (Reader Pro). * Securely connect Amazon Q Business to your business knowledge and data * Receive permission-aware responses in a conversational interface (responses up to approximately seven pages) * Use secure and seamless sign-on with enterprise login * Create new content quickly * Gain fast insights on your uploaded files * Gain data insights with Amazon Q in QuickSight (Reader Pro) * Custom and fully managed plugins for popular third-party applications * Get images as responses if you choose to select image processing * Integrate seamlessly in Slack, Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Teams * Access Q Business through the web browser extension Amazon Q Apps: * Easily create, publish, and share apps * Choose the data sources for each app card * Create and consume Amazon Q Apps outputs with APIs |","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/q/business/pricing/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AI Assistant","context":"## Amazon Q Services\n\n### Amazon Q Business\n\nWith Amazon Q Business, you pay for user subscriptions and index capacity. Amazon Q Business pricing offers two subscription models—Amazon Q Business Lite and Amazon Q Business Pro—so you can choose the right plan for everyone in your company. The Amazon Q Business Lite subscription of $3 per user/month provides users access to basic functionality such as asking questions and receiving permission-aware responses. The Amazon Q Business Pro subscription of $20 per user/month provides users access to the full suite of Amazon Q Business capabilities, including access to Amazon Q Apps, and Amazon Q in QuickSight (Reader Pro).\n\nExplore Amazon Q Business pricing\n\n### Amazon Q Developer\n\nAmazon Q Developer reimagines the experience across the entire software development lifecycle, making it faster and easier to build, secure, manage, and optimize applications on or off of AWS. The Amazon Q Developer Free Tier lets users code faster with code suggestions in the IDE and CLI and review code licenses with reference tracking, as well as free public CLI completions and limited access to advanced features. The Amazon Q Developer Pro Tier offers all that as well as the ability to manage users and policies with enterprise access controls; customize Amazon Q to your code base to get even better suggestions; and high limits of advanced features.\n\nExplore Amazon Q Developer pricing","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/q/pricing/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"QBusiness: New-QBUSApplication Cmdlet | AWS Tools for PowerShell","context":"## Description\n\nCreates an Amazon Q Business application.\nThere are new tiers for Amazon Q Business. Not all features in Amazon Q Business Pro are also available in Amazon Q Business Lite. For information on what's included in Amazon Q Business Lite and what's included in Amazon Q Business Pro, see Amazon Q Business tiers. You must use the Amazon Q Business console to assign subscription tiers to users.\nAn Amazon Q Apps service linked role will be created if it's absent in the Amazon Web Services account when QAppsConfiguration is enabled in the request. For more information, see Using service-linked roles for Q Apps.\nWhen you create an application, Amazon Q Business may securely transmit data for processing from your selected Amazon Web Services region, but within your geography. For more information, see Cross region inference in Amazon Q Business","url":"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/powershell/v4/reference/index.html?page=New-QBUSApplication.html&tocid=New-QBUSApplication"}]}}

